    "text_full": "Skip to content\nUnofficial Royalty\nThe Site for Royal Information and News\nHOME ABOUT US CURRENT MONARCHIES FORMER MONARCHIES ROYAL NEWS RECAP UPCOMING ROYAL EVENTS COLUMN ARCHIVES CROWNS, REGALIA CURRENT ROYAL FAMILIES PROFILES LINES OF SUCCESSION MONARCHS, HEIRS, SUCCESSION PEERAGE, NOBILITY ROYAL CEREMONIES, EVENTS ROYAL CHRISTENINGS ROYAL CHURCHES ROYAL DATES ROYAL DEATHS, ILLNESSES ROYAL FUNERALS, BURIALS ROYAL ORDERS, HONORS ROYAL RELATIONSHIPS ROYAL RESIDENCES ROYAL SOCIAL MEDIA, ADDRESSES ROYAL TIDBITS ROYAL WEDDINGS THE GREAT PRETENDERS TITLES, STYLES PRIVACY\nRoyal Ceremonies and Events\n\nCoronation of King George VI and Queen Elizabeth, 1937; Credit – Wikipedia\n\nRoyal ceremonies and events run from births to deaths and various events in between. Sometimes they evolve around a personal event that even non-royal people experience, like a wedding. Sometimes royal ceremonies are directly related to the role of royalty, like a coronation.\n\nWhich Monarchies Have Coronations? What Succession Ceremonies Do Other Monarchies Have?\n\nUnited Kingdom\n\nBritish Royal Christenings\nBritish Coronations\nBritish Royal Funerals\nBritish Royal Weddings\nChanging the Guard (daily)\nChelsea Flower Show (five days in May)\nChristmas Message (December 25)\nCommonwealth Day (2nd Monday in March)\nDiplomatic Reception (held in December)\nGarden Parties (late spring and summer)\nGarter Day (in June, the Monday before Royal Ascot)\nInvestitures (throughout the year)\nNational Service of Remembrance (2nd Sunday in November or the Sunday nearest to November 11)\nRoyal Ascot (June)\nRoyal Maundy Service (Holy Thursday)\nState Opening of Parliament (the beginning of a new session of Parliament)\nTrooping the Colour (usually a Saturday in June)\n\nKingdom of Belgium\n\nAccession To The Throne\nBelgian National Day (July 21)\nBelgian Royal Christenings\nBelgian Royal Weddings\nCommemoration for Deceased Members of the Belgian Royal Family (on/around February 1